ry_overlap":[{"category":"Restaurants","historical_business_count":8},{"category":"Bars","historical_business_count":5},{"category":"Wine Bars","historical_business_count":0},{"category":"American (New)","historical_business_count":2},{"category":"Nightlife","historical_business_count":5}],"history":[{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"American (New), Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"American (New), Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"3TNpd3OD2a6DZcx9DI9Olw","review_id":"27WZK_LoQhucBrRKYRgZ4A","date":"2011-06-24T17:04:21","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9364714622497559,"text_excerpt":"This review is based on my first experience at Bouche--but I went to dinner with a repeat offender who is absolutely smitten by the place. The atmosphere is absolutely amazing--they've done a tremendous job on the interior, with brick highlights, open wine storage, and glass classes with things that make you wish you had a hammer and a get-away car---like Louis XIII cognac. I'm kidding. Maybe. One of my dining companions arrived early and texted that she was waiting in the cigar bar--an attached but isolated section of the restaurant. First thought: uh oh. Experience: totally different. Amazing ventilation in that room! I didn't want to leave. Service: Absolutely top drawer. So much so th..."},{"business_id":"3TNpd3OD2a6DZcx9DI9Olw","review_id":"AAH3gnwsv2QXuAQ_kZG_Mw","date":"2010-07-01T16:49:21","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9232945442199707,"text_excerpt":"I attended a wine tasting event here last week and was so impressed with this new Warehouse District restaurant. They were giving out taster sizes of all the dishes on the menu and every bite was delightful! I can not wait to go back for dinner. I would also consider using this place as a group dinner or lunch. The private dining room is cozy and elegant and the cigar room next to it is a really nice touch. Overall, this is a great addition to the New Orleans dining scene. Check it out."},{"business_id":"3TNpd3OD2a6DZcx9DI9Olw","review_id":"53SVPCoaXJB0hncSGrBtCQ","date":"2011-06-22T18:39:55","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.8934041261672974,"text_excerpt":"An exclusive, trendy atmosphere---- Very upscale and eschelon for a bar spot! Their truffled mac and cheese is almost better than mine. The strawberry and pomegranate mojitos are a bit pricey at 14 bucks but well worth the charge!"}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
